    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-067 — JPEG decode via gdk-pixbuf.** Closes the last visible Wikipedia gap: Tim Berners-Lee photo now renders in History section.\n\n**Production-verified (fixture screenshot 2026-11-04).**\n\n## The verified delta\n\n4-row fixture at `docs/adr067-jpeg-test.html`:\n\n| Row | Content | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Tim Berners-Lee JPEG (Wikimedia CDN) | **Renders, colors correct** (natural skin, blue tie, grey suit) |\n| 2 | HTML5 logo PNG | Renders (regression clean) |\n| 3 | Wikipedia wordmark SVG | Renders (regression clean) |\n| 4 | Tim photo at 100px width | Renders at correct size (scale verified) |\n\n## The fix\n\nJPEG magic-byte branch (3 bytes `FF D8 FF`, covers JFIF / EXIF / raw) between PNG and SVG dispatch. Decode via `gdk_pixbuf_new_from_stream` + manual RGBA→ARGB32 pixel copy with R↔B channel swap.\n\nThe channel swap keeps `honeybee_lib` GTK-free — `gdk_cairo_surface_create_from_pixbuf` (GDK4) isn't available in the library, only in the executable. Manual pixel copy was the layering-correct choice.\n\n## The stub incident (honest)\n\nDuring ADR-068's crash isolation, a `// DIAG-067: temporarily disabled` + `return nullptr;` was inserted at the top of the JPEG branch. The crash turned out to be pure GTK4/GSK. The stub was supposed to be removed but carried through the branch switch + stash/rebase dance.\n\n**The `.o` file showed zero gdk_pixbuf symbols** because the branch returned immediately before the decode call. Two rounds of debugging chased phantom causes before `grep 'DIAG-067'` located the actual cause.\n\n**Lesson recorded in ADR**: after using temporary early-returns for crash isolation, `grep` for the diagnostic marker before merging the branch.\n\n## What this closes\n\n- **The last visible Wikipedia gap** — Tim photo now renders\n- **All raster formats work**: PNG (existing Cairo decoder) + JPEG (new gdk-pixbuf decoder)\n- ADR-063's deferred visual verification was already unblocked by ADR-066's text readability fix — now the photo completes the visual delta\n\n## What's deferred\n\n- GIF / WebP / TIFF (gdk-pixbuf supports them, no consumer)\n- EXIF orientation (image rotated wrong if EXIF rotation present)\n- Format auto-detection (route all non-SVG through gdk-pixbuf — future ADR)\n\n## Test count\n\n691 / 2641 unchanged (no new tests; fixture verification is the primary proof).\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Production-visual, fixture-screenshot verified.**\n\nRefs #272\n",
